SHAPE: ONE program, ONE branch, a lever-set policy on the sampler. I reject lens 1's two-program variant (ROUTER_MAIN + ROUTER_MAIN_BAKEAWARE). Its motivating worry is real — planet-lod-tributary-patch.js:343 reads through HEIGHT_FRAG unconditionally and an in-place edit would flip it to the baked body at the shipped default — but a second exported program breaks the identity assertion that makes AC-POSCTRL-FIELD possible ("the instrument runs literally the program the router runs"). The policy approach gets both: one program, and the tributary patch explicitly pinned to today's body.

VERIFIED PRECONDITIONS (grepped, not assumed): HEIGHT_GLSL already declares everything the branch needs — planet-lod-height.glsl.js:149 `uniform float uReliefBakeStrength;`, :150 `uniform samplerCube uReliefBakeCube;`, :151 `vec4 sampleBakedRelief(vec3 dir){ return textureCube(uReliefBakeCube, normalize(dir)); }`. planet-lod-rivers.js:358 `export const HEIGHT_FRAG = HEIGHT_GLSL + ROUTER_MAIN;` already links them; ROUTER_MAIN simply never references them. createHeightSampler binds the live object by reference (planet-lod-rivers.js:439 `vertexShader: HEIGHT_VERT, fragmentShader: HEIGHT_FRAG, uniforms,`) and the lab pushes the real cube at world-engine-lab.html:3892. HEIGHT_VERT writes `vObjN = normalize(aDir);` (planet-lod-rivers.js:302) matching the lab's `vObjN = normalize(position);` on unit-sphere geometry. So: ZERO new uniforms, ZERO new GLSL functions, ZERO change to planet-lod-height.glsl.js. The brief's feared mesh-node topology problem never binds — the cube is direction-keyed.

═══ 1. planet-lod-rivers.js — ROUTER_MAIN, replacing the single line at :323 ═══

  export const ROUTER_MAIN = `
    void main(){
      initProvinces(vPos);
      float canyonHeight = 0.0;
      float fluvialWet = 0.0;
      float fwBase = 0.0;
      // SPLIT-TRAP #5 extended to the READBACK program. The router's AND the instrument's
      // height source is now gated on the SAME uReliefBakeStrength uniform the renderer gates
      // on (the if/else in the lab's own main()) — one body, no surface-vs-readback split.
      // Transplanted VERBATIM from world-engine-lab.html so the two can never drift apart.
      // strength 0 => ELSE branch = the verbatim pre-AC2 fbmd line, NO textureCube fetch.
      // route() only ever calls sampler.read() on that branch, so routing is byte-identical.
      vec4 hd;
      if (uReliefBakeStrength > 0.0) {
        vec4 baked = sampleBakedRelief(vObjN);          // object-space direction-keyed, seam-free
        vec4 synth = fbmd(vPos, uOctaves, fwBase);      // in-shader DETAIL residual
        hd = vec4(baked.x * uReliefBakeStrength, baked.yzw * uReliefBakeStrength)
           + synth * (1.0 - uReliefBakeStrength);
      } else {
        hd = fbmd(vPos, uOctaves, fwBase);              // VERBATIM pre-AC2 path, NO cube fetch
      }
      float h = hd.x;
      vec3 grad = hd.yzw;
      vec3 gradBase = hd.yzw;
      // …combiner chain from mountainCombiner through deltaCombiner UNCHANGED, byte-for-byte…
      gl_FragColor = vec4(h, grad);
    }
  `;
  export const HEIGHT_FRAG = HEIGHT_GLSL + ROUTER_MAIN;   // unchanged: still ONE program

NOTE: `gradBase` still snapshots hd.yzw AFTER the branch, exactly as the lab does (world-engine-lab.html:392), so massWastCombiner's base-gradient contract is preserved. FENCE: this file is in tests/vis-scale-fence.test.js:55's procgenSurfaces list and the grep covers comments — the words visScaleOf / sVis / VIS_SCALE_EXP must not appear. Say "the display crossover" or "the effective bake strength the lab frame loop writes". Never add an allowlist entry.

Also in planet-lod-rivers.js:
- :422 `createHeightSampler({ renderer, uniforms, verts, octavesDuringRead = 9, bodyPolicy = 'live' })`.
- :452-465 `read()` — wrap the whole pin/restore in try/finally (ride-along [16], now a PRECONDITION: once read() forces a body-selecting uniform, a mid-read throw leaves the RENDERED planet on the wrong body, a failure class that cannot exist today); add uLodRamp to the saved set ([15]); pin per policy inside the window:
    'live' / 'rendered' -> pin nothing beyond {uOctaves, uFwClamp, uLodRamp}. Byte-identical to today.
    'synth'   -> additionally uReliefBakeStrength = 0.0, uDispDomainScale = 1.0
    'carrier' -> additionally uReliefBakeStrength = 1.0, uDispDomainScale = 1.0
- `read()` returns `{ height, grad, provenance }` where provenance is captured INSIDE the window: { bodyPolicy, reliefBakeStrength, dispDomainScale, octaves, lodRamp, heightSource: strength > 0 ? 'carrier' : 'sampler' }. Purely additive — route() (:1375) and the tributary patch destructure only height/grad.

═══ 2. planet-lod-tributary-patch.js:343 ═══
Pass `bodyPolicy: 'synth'`. This EXPLICITLY preserves today's behaviour (100% synth at octave 12, the sub-base-mesh detail the fine dendrites grow on) instead of silently flipping it to a body band-limited to ~113 km. Declared NON-GOAL: the tributary patch has the same SPLIT-TRAP fault as [1] in a second consumer; it is latent (patchStrength defaults 0.0, world-engine-lab.html:1541) and fixing it is a visible behaviour change that must not ride inside a measurement fix.

═══ 3. src/worldengine/instrument/fieldSampler.js ═══
- `sampleEquirect` / `samplePatch` gain `body` ('rendered' | 'carrier' | 'synth'), REQUIRED at the sweep layer, defaulting to 'rendered' at the raw-call layer. Cache key gains the body (one sampler per policy).
- `samplePatch` gains `spanDeg`, mutually exclusive with `spanKm`: spanKm = spanDeg * (PI/180) * radiusEarth * 6371, computed at the call site — NO sampling.js change needed (patchDirections at sampling.js:127 already converts spanKm to an angle via `spanAngX = spanKmX / R`).
  WHY: the carrier lives on a FIXED 40,000-node unit-sphere mesh (planet-lod-rivers.js:59 `TARGET_N: 40000,`, built once in ensureMesh at :1277). Node spacing = sqrt(4*pi/40000) = 0.0177 rad = 1.014 deg, so the smallest resolvable form is ~2 deg (~226 km at R=1). The banked 2000 km / 128 px patch samples at 15.6 km/px — six times below the carrier's Nyquist at R=1 — and at R=16 that same 2000 km window spans only ~1.1 node spacings. A km-fixed patch is degenerate on the carrier. Angular-span patches for every pinned-lever body; keep the km-span patch only for body:'rendered', where screen size is the meaningful frame.
- Sample object carries `body` + `provenance`; `describeSample` emits them under a `control` key — NOT top level, so they can never be fitted.
- CORRECT the header at :10-12. "what we measure is what the planet is actually rendering" is load-bearing and, as written, reads as a body guarantee it did not hold. Restate it as the mechanism guarantee it actually is (live uniforms, no drift) and name the body axis explicitly.
- FENCE: this file is inside the src/worldengine walk at tests/vis-scale-fence.test.js:64-69, comments included. Name the field `dispDomainScale`, never `visScale`. (fieldProbe's existing `meta.visScale` at world-engine-lab.html:6930 is legal only because it lives in the lab HTML — do not move that line into the module.)

═══ 4. src/worldengine/instrument/sweep.js ═══
- META_NAMESPACES (:157) += 'control'. Move `radiusEarth` off the top level of describeSample's return (fieldSampler.js:151) into control — this is ride-along [17], and it DELETES the banked "radiusEarth control" row, which is why the replacement must land in the same increment.
- Add the CONFOUND pass: after a sweep, fit every numeric `control.*` field against the driver exactly as descriptors are fitted. Any body-defining lever with a resolvably non-zero exponent => the result carries `confounded: [lever, ...]` and every fit inherits the list. On the banked R = 0.5..16 sweep this fires immediately on BOTH reliefBakeStrength (1.0 -> 0.5 -> 0.0) and dispDomainScale (proportional to R^0.5). This is the control that would actually have caught [1] at R1 time — unlike a body-identity check, which would have been GREEN at every AC-CURVE point because the crossover is 0 there.

═══ 5. world-engine-lab.html ═══
- `sampleField` (:6905) / `fieldProbe` (:6914): pass `body` through; return `control` alongside `meta`; hard-check `control.heightSource` against `riverOverlay.heightSource` (getter exists, planet-lod-rivers.js:1440) and refuse to bank on disagreement.
- `responseCurve` (:6959): default probe becomes angular-span for pinned bodies; census path takes `bodies: ['carrier','rendered']` and measures both at each swept point.
- setPoint (:6969-6974): schedule and AWAIT an explicit route. Today the carrier is re-baked only as a side effect of setSeed (updateSeedUniforms -> riverRerouteDebounced, world-engine-lab.html:2488). A fixed-seed radius sweep would read a carrier baked at the PREVIOUS radius and report exponent 0 with a clean r^2.
- Console `_lab` API ONLY. No lil-gui control — adding one forfeits the taxonomy exemption written at world-engine-lab.html:180 and pulls in tests/planet-archetypes.test.js.

